### SmartRetailX auth flow
### Run against gateway (default) or point host at a single service.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@productId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### 1. Register customer
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "shopper@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "name": "Shopper",
  "role": "customer"
}

### 2. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "shopper@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Capture tokens (REST Client / VS Code)
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 3. Access protected order endpoint (customer — allowed)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [{ "productId": "{{productId}}", "quantity": 1 }],
  "paymentMethod": "card"
}

### 4. Wrong role → 403 (customer cannot mutate catalogue)
POST {{baseUrl}}/catalogue/api/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Fail"
}

### 5. Refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/users/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### 6. No token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/api/v1/orders
